==Russian==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ru|orv|вѣдѣ}}. Russian [[ведь]] is a former {{etyl|ine-pro|ru}} root [[perfect tense|perfect]] {{m|ine-pro|*wóyd-}} with [[mediopassive]] ending ''-ai'', with meaning "I have seen". Cognate with {{etyl|en|-}} [[wit]] (to wit).

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA}}
* {{audio|Ru-ведь.ogg|audio|lang=ru}}

===Interjection===
{{head|ru|interjection}}

# [[after all]]
# [[indeed]], [[surely]]
# [[why]], [[well]]
# [[then]], you know, you see
# isn’t it?
#: {{ux|ru|Ведь [[уже|уже́]] [[поздно|по́здно]]|It’s late, isn’t it?|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|ru|Ведь [[он]] [[знаток|знато́к]]|After all, he’s an expert.|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|ru|Ведь [[я]] [[вы|вам]] [[говорить|говори́л]]!|But I told you!|inline=1}}

===Conjunction===
{{head|ru|conjunction}}

# you see, [[you know]]
#: {{ux|ru|[[он|Он]] [[лежать|лежи́т]], ведь он [[на]] [[прошлый|про́шлой]] [[неделя|неде́ле]] [[заболеть|заболе́л]]|He’s in bed...he fell ill last week, you know.}}

